Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.1 item shop (STITSHOP) panels hang from the 16:9 edges

OLED feedback on preview.47 (US): "the item shop is still 4:3". Patch 0053
gave the shop the menu gutter and a background that fills it, but every panel
stayed where the game puts it, in the middle 320 columns, so the screen looked
4:3 with a patterned border. This does for the shop what 0076 did for the field
menu and 0102 for the card packs shop. Drawing positions only, gated on the
gutter (DW3_MENU_LEFT / DW3_MENU_RIGHT are the PS1 values with widescreen off).

- shop.c: the money bar, the BUY / SELL panel and the back plate (with their
  windows, cursor and open pivots) one gutter further right.
- item_list.c: the list's frame is a full-width band, widened to both edges
  (DW3_MENU_BAND).
- info.c: the item plate (name, Equip, Items) is extended to the right edge,
  the description band widened, the stats page's left plate and its hint one
  gutter further left. The three partner boxes stay in the middle.
- trade.c: the buy and sell dialogs' panels (quantity, total, Buy / No, the
  four sale kinds, the message) with their windows, arrows and cursors one
  gutter further right.

